From 9da9a4bb0325a49775c663109c1acedc504811dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:05:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] skins: give every skin the player information of Hades, from
 Estuary's pages

Estuary shows the player information of Hades in its
DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml: the overview page (the source, Dolby Vision
and HDR, what the display is sent, the drawing) and the Dolby Vision page.
Their values are the properties hades.* of the Home window, which any skin
can read, but what makes them readable (the variables that turn their codes
into words, the maps of codec names, the strings, the row includes) is
Estuary's: with another skin there is none of it.

system/hades/HadesIncludes.xml now holds those variables, maps and
includes, and every skin is given it after its own includes
(CSkinInfo::LoadIncludes()). A definition of the skin's with the same name
is the one that counts (CGUIIncludes keeps the first), so Estuary is as it
was, and another skin can show $VAR[HadesDVOutputVar], $VAR[HadesDVReasonVar],
$VAR[HadesOutSignalVar] and the rest, or use the includes HadesInfoRow and
HadesInfoHeading. Estuary's generic names that another skin may use for
something else are given Hades' own (HadesVideoCodecVar, HadesCodecMap...).

It is made from Estuary's own files by tools/hades-playerinfo/
make-playerinfo.py, so there is one source: Estuary's strings as
$ADDON[skin.estuary n] (the skin is always installed, and its translations
come with it), its colours as values (a name another skin does not have is
no colour), its textures copied to system/hades. The same script makes the
dialog that shows the two pages in a skin without them (the next commit),
and with --check says whether system/hades is what it would make.

Checked on the host (pi_check.py): system/hades is what the script makes;
both files are well-formed; the 31 variables and 3 maps that are named are
all there; the 135 strings are Estuary's, in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx;
the 4 textures are there and every colour is a value; each variable is
Estuary's, value for value; and the dialog has the 73 rows of the overview
page and the 17 of the Dolby Vision page, label for label. Six mutations
each make it fail. Not verified: any of it in Kodi with another skin.
